// `String_Builder`: repeated appends into one growing buffer, finished as one
// immutable `string`.
//
// Borrowing iterators: split, fields, and lines.
//
// None of these allocates. Every part borrows the text it was built from, so it
// cannot outlive it — which is exactly what a `string_view` already promises.
// Each is an ordinary iteration protocol implementation, so `foreach` walks it
// and generic code sees the same `Element`/`Iterator`/`iter`/`next` members a
// built-in container contributes.
//
// UTF-8 algorithms and efficient construction.
//
// The built-in `string` already owns validation, byte and rune counts,
// comparison, slicing, concatenation, rune iteration and the conversions. This
// package adds what those primitives do not: search, trimming, splitting,
// joining, and a builder that turns repeated appends into one allocation.
//
// Every index and length here is a **byte offset**. A name says `rune` when it
// means a scalar value; nothing in this package counts graphemes.
